KNOWNBUG
assignment-to-non-constant-index3.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.v1\[\$past\(main\.i\) \+ 4\] == 1\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(##1 main\.v2\[\$past\(main\.i\)\] == 1\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The RTL construction rewrites a bit-select with a non-constant index
on the left-hand side into a with-expression on the whole vector,
using the Verilog index as is. Neither the offset of the declared
range nor its direction are taken into account, as done when lowering
reads, and hence the write and the read of the bit disagree on the
bit position.
